=head1 DESCRIPTION

Specifies whether the domain should encrypt data at rest, and if so,
the Key Management Service (KMS) key to use. Can only be used when
creating a new domain or enabling encryption at rest for the first time
on an existing domain. You can't modify this parameter after it's
already been specified.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 Enabled => Bool

True to enable encryption at rest.


=head2 KmsKeyId => Str

The KMS key ID. Takes the form C<1a2a3a4-1a2a-3a4a-5a6a-1a2a3a4a5a6a>.



